{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773099960,"nonce":"QD0KtoRr292Pw6rrfrdh2Nd+Rq4=","title":"Network composite exposes misleading fixed 64-dim internal template — violates graph-as-model principle","message":"The Network composite (is_composite: true) shows an internal template with encoder MLP + GRU core (64x64) + decoder MLP when entered. These internal dimensions are hardcoded in createNetworkSubgraph() and are NOT the model that actually gets trained. The worker builds the model from the outer Network node params (hidden_size, input_size, out_size), ignoring the internal template entirely.\n\nThis violates the core principle: the graph IS the model. From the user perspective, there should be no discrepancy between what they see and what is built/trained.\n\nOptions to fix:\n1. Remove Network from _compositeTypes — make it a simple non-composite node where users directly edit hidden_size/input_size/out_size\n2. Propagate outer params into inner nodes so the template stays in sync\n3. Replace the Network abstraction entirely with explicit GRU+MLP nodes\n\nOption 1 is simplest and most correct for the current state of the Studio.","files":null}]}